      <p style="font-size:1rem;color:#a1a1aa;margin:0 0 24px;line-height:1.75;max-width:700px">Some PDFs open perfectly but will not let you print them, copy a line of text, fill in the form, or use a screen reader. That is an owner password setting permission flags, and it is a different thing from a password that stops the file opening. Upload your document and you will see a plain list of exactly what it allows and blocks — then remove the restrictions in one click and download an unrestricted copy. Free, no sign-up, no watermark, and nothing is uploaded.</p>
      <p id="seo-direct-answer" style="font-size:0.95rem;color:#e4e4e7;background:#18181b;border-left:3px solid #60a5fa;border-radius:0 8px 8px 0;padding:14px 18px;margin:0 0 28px;line-height:1.7;max-width:720px">A PDF that opens fine but refuses to print or let you copy text is carrying owner-password permission flags. Those flags are advisory rather than encryption, so re-saving the document without its encryption dictionary clears them. On ihatepdf, upload the PDF and you are first shown exactly which actions it blocks, then one click removes the restrictions and downloads an unrestricted copy. Free, no sign-up, and the file is never uploaded. This does not apply to a PDF that demands a password before it will open — that is genuine encryption and needs the password.</p>
      <div style="display:flex;flex-wrap:wrap;gap:8px;margin-bottom:32px">
        <span style="background:#18181b;border:1px solid #27272a;border-radius:999px;padding:4px 12px;font-size:0.78rem;color:#a1a1aa">&#x2713; 100% Free</span>
        <span style="background:#18181b;border:1px solid #27272a;border-radius:999px;padding:4px 12px;font-size:0.78rem;color:#a1a1aa">&#x2713; No Watermark</span>
        <span style="background:#18181b;border:1px solid #27272a;border-radius:999px;padding:4px 12px;font-size:0.78rem;color:#a1a1aa">&#x2713; No Sign-Up</span>
        <span style="background:#18181b;border:1px solid #27272a;border-radius:999px;padding:4px 12px;font-size:0.78rem;color:#a1a1aa">&#x2713; No Upload — Files Stay on Your Device</span>
        <span style="background:#18181b;border:1px solid #27272a;border-radius:999px;padding:4px 12px;font-size:0.78rem;color:#a1a1aa">&#x2713; Works Offline</span>
